#: ../../../developer/releases/version-scheme.rst:3
#: 8f89798fb0fa4ed3a6669074adac51f7
msgid "Version scheme"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/releases/version-scheme.rst:6
#: 1c3dda06969c46da8d197757025aafcf
msgid ""
"The Qubes OS Project uses the `semantic versioning <https://semver.org/>`__ "
"standard. Version numbers are written as ``<major>.<minor>.<patch>``. When "
"``<patch>`` is omitted (e.g., ``4.1``), it is usually either because "
"``<patch>`` is zero (as in ``4.1.0``) or because we are referring to a "
"specific minor release irrespective of any particular patch release within "
"it. Similarly, the major release number alone (e.g., ``R4``) is sometimes "
"used to refer to an entire release series inclusive of all minor and patch "
"releases within it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/releases/version-scheme.rst:8
#: 3dc7efdce1ce496ab03858324cfa594b
msgid ""
"In general, patch releases are for backward-compatible bug fixes, minor "
"releases are for backward-compatible enhancements and new features, and "
"major release are for any backward-incompatible changes. This means that, in "
"general, one should *not* try to introduce features or enhancements in patch "
"releases or any backward-incompatible changes in patch or minor releases. "
"(Templates are a notable exception, as upstream OSes almost always have "
"their own release schedules.) Bug fixes are allowed in all releases, and "
"backward-compatible changes are allowed in all major and minor releases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/releases/version-scheme.rst:10
#: 3a4fd12b606342209457306b2342a129
msgid ""
"Qubes OS minor releases generally include new features, new templates, and "
"occasionally new defaults, but they are still backward-compatible in the "
"sense that qubes and features that worked in the previous release still "
"function, though the UI may be different in some cases. In general, "
"deprecated features are removed only in major releases, and in-place "
"upgrades between major versions are not guaranteed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/releases/version-scheme.rst:12
#: 90a5143171d34ab58d465f1b979f8191
msgid ""
"Following standard practice, **version** refers to any build that has been "
"assigned a version name or number, e.g., ``3.2-rc2``, ``4.0.4``, ``4.1-"
"beta1``. By contrast, **release** refers to any version that is intended for "
"consumption by the general userbase. For example, ``4.0.4`` was both a "
"**version** and a **release**, since it was stable and intended for general "
"public use, while ``4.1-beta1`` was a **version** but *not* a **release**, "
"since it was not stable and was intended only for :doc:`testing </user/"
"downloading-installing-upgrading/testing>`. All releases are versions, but "
"not all versions are releases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/releases/version-scheme.rst:14
#: 5eadf47ec0d949b9a215638c46be206c
msgid ""
"The letter **R**, as in ``R4.1``, stands for **release**. The abbreviation "
"**RC**, as in ``3.2-rc2``, stands for **release candidate**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/releases/version-scheme.rst:17
#: 5bee16b53fd645e19723ef15fd4e665f
msgid "Qubes distributions and products"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/releases/version-scheme.rst:20
#: 4876de0f95234ab58872fc0fbebf3931
msgid ""
"We intend to make it easy to make a remix of Qubes, targeting another "
"hypervisor or isolation provider. We may also create commercial products "
"intended for specific circumstances. There is one distinguished distribution "
"called **Qubes OS**. All source code for it is available for download under "
"a :doc:`free and open-source license </developer/code/license>` and is "
"openly developed on `GitHub <https://github.com/QubesOS>`__ and "
"our :doc:`mailing lists </introduction/support>`. The rest of this document "
"discusses Qubes OS. Another remix may have its own version series."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/releases/version-scheme.rst:23
#: 36d7a05d0e31495b8761bd8aaf6779f9
msgid "Release versioning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/releases/version-scheme.rst:26
#: 02bc0642ba3c4893935afe24852198e6
msgid ""
"Qubes OS as a whole is released from time to time. When preparing a new "
"release, we decide on the ``<major>.<minor>`` numbers (e.g., ``3.0``, which "
"is short for ``3.0.0``). We then publish the first release candidate, e.g., "
"``3.0.0-rc1``. When we feel that enough progress has been made, we’ll "
"release ``3.0.0-rc2`` and so on. All these versions (which are not yet "
"releases) are considered unstable and are not intended for production use. "
"You are welcome to :doc:`help us test </user/downloading-installing-"
"upgrading/testing>` these versions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/releases/version-scheme.rst:28
#: e44e1945a8aa4fd195f20708b824fb0f
msgid ""
"When enough progress has been made, we announce the first stable release, "
"e.g. ``3.0.0``. This is not only a version but an actual release. It is "
"considered stable, and we commit to supporting it according to "
"our :doc:`support schedule </user/downloading-installing-upgrading/supported-"
"releases>`. Core components are branched at this moment, and bug fixes are "
"backported from the main branch. Please see :doc:`help, support, mailing "
"lists, and forum </introduction/support>` for places to ask questions about "
"stable releases. No major features or interface incompatibilities are to be "
"included in this release. We release bug fixes as patch releases (``3.0.1``, "
"``3.0.2``, and so on), while backward-compatible enhancements and new "
"features are introduced in the next minor release (e.g., ``3.1``). Any "
"backward-incompatible changes are introduced in the next major release "
"(e.g., ``4.0``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/releases/version-scheme.rst:30
#: ebfbfeccc6bf4b78a6826c40b2aca906
msgid ""
"Please see :doc:`issue tracking </introduction/issue-tracking>` for "
"information about how releases are handled in the issue tracker."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/releases/version-scheme.rst:35
#: e812870fe9d441899bd24507adacd122
msgid "Release schedule policy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/releases/version-scheme.rst:38
#: 253717cef0734048b4b5d04e81880da6
msgid ""
"There is **no specific schedule for releases** other than a general roadmap. "
"When the time comes, we declare a feature freeze, tag ``-rc1``, and release "
"an ISO. From this point on, no new features are accepted, and our schedule "
"begins."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/releases/version-scheme.rst:40
#: f7b7b8d68fd445f0aa97e51d0d62a890
msgid "Each release candidate period is as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/releases/version-scheme.rst:42
#: f516379f21af40249a4137942636307c
msgid ""
"For the first two weeks, **we accept and assign bug reports** to be fixed "
"before the next release candidate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/releases/version-scheme.rst:43
#: 4c637863aef14b88b0c8ea930930226a
msgid ""
"For the next two weeks, we generally **focus on fixing assigned bug "
"reports**, so issues discovered during this period may be postponed until a "
"later RC."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/releases/version-scheme.rst:44
#: 4cdb156cbbcb49c385f5c6e0d2d36723
msgid ""
"Finally, there is a one week current-testing freeze, during which time **no "
"new packages are released**, in the hope that they will be installed and "
"tested by wider user base."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/releases/version-scheme.rst:51
#: f51d877998bc4b5a911486959b658246
msgid "Stage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/releases/version-scheme.rst:52
#: d110a664e31a46979f94f48301583f04
msgid "Duration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/releases/version-scheme.rst:53
#: 21101a4fb7b049aa8d4182168377b1a4
msgid "initial testing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/releases/version-scheme.rst:54
#: ../../../developer/releases/version-scheme.rst:56
#: 15bd3f9c8ca044c98c9536de7ba8a09c 7a4bb984ad90448c8596783786c1809f
msgid "two weeks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/releases/version-scheme.rst:55
#: 8f2de072d32242c79e4b327b83f0ac45
msgid "bug fixing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/releases/version-scheme.rst:57
#: 5fab1e35fec94f18885660a2727eeb75
msgid "``current-testing`` freeze"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/releases/version-scheme.rst:58
#: 46b97b65f89040a99535efa24db02d25
msgid "one week"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/releases/version-scheme.rst:60
#: cca07ec7ca394762be20a8ed6076e8dc
msgid ""
"The next RC is usually **released five weeks after the former**. All "
"packages are published in the ``current`` repository, and the cycle starts "
"over. There should always be at least one release candidate before the final "
"release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/releases/version-scheme.rst:62
#: e00352c6ea604eef84b5255e424f9e8f
msgid ""
"Starting with the second cycle (that is, after ``-rc1``), two weeks into the "
"cycle (after the primary bug-reporting period), we decide whether there "
"should be another RC. If, based on the bugs that have been reported, we "
"decide that the latest RC will be designated as the stable release, then we "
"decide on its release date, which should be no more than one week later."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/releases/version-scheme.rst:64
#: d362715b53f84216b4a5576fad02f91c
msgid "To get a real life example, check the :doc:`4_1/schedule`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/releases/version-scheme.rst:66
#: d80ba16bb64a42eba82345bbfb520196
msgid "|Release cycle|"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/releases/version-scheme.rst:112
#: db185dc8a547449f91b348f4cb279ea5
msgid "Release cycle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/releases/version-scheme.rst:69
#: 067ea5ccfad54009ab6c7195b13cfa3e
msgid "Bug priorities"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/releases/version-scheme.rst:72
#: 036b9d082c5d471ab18ed18346cd414c
msgid ""
"When deciding whether the current release candidate is the final one, the "
"Committee takes bug :ref:`priorities <introduction/issue-tracking:priority>` "
"into consideration. The meaning of them is as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/releases/version-scheme.rst:74
#: eb1148fc5220429481f9c53566781632
msgid ""
"``blocker`` — when any such bug is present in the current release candidate, "
"it can’t be considered final release. Bugs with this priority must be fixed "
"before the next release candidate, even if that means delaying its release "
"(which should be considered only last resort option)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/releases/version-scheme.rst:76
#: 3ce3a53c301249bb81cd36ae32900bef
msgid ""
"``critical`` — when any such bug is present in the current release "
"candidate, it can’t be considered final release. But such bugs are not "
"qualified to delay next release candidate release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/releases/version-scheme.rst:78
#: 534b851091c145468e67cadcb0c52347
msgid ""
"``major`` — existence of such bugs do not strictly prevent the current "
"release candidate be considered final (but of course we should try hard to "
"not have them there). Fixing bugs of this priority can be delayed and "
"qualified as updates to the final stable release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/releases/version-scheme.rst:80
#: 93ad637fb43f45368cc9d9101d727d3d
msgid ""
"``default`` and ``minor`` — existence of such bugs do not prevent the "
"current release candidate be considered final. Fixing such bugs can be "
"delayed to the next Qubes OS release. Eventually such fixes might be "
"backported as an update to the stable release(s). (``default`` should really "
"be assigned a more specific priority, but in practice there are too many "
"issues and not enough time, so ``default`` ends up staying on many issues.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/releases/version-scheme.rst:84
#: 8439650fcf314a748945d09a5624d3cb
msgid ""
"All above is about bugs, no features should be assigned to the current "
"release after first ``-rc``. Supreme Committee is free to adjust priorities "
"appropriately."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/releases/version-scheme.rst:87
#: b42c2d69def34177934107fba2cf0384
msgid "Component version"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/releases/version-scheme.rst:90
#: dc29fc693acd41019a3d2056f0d6af3b
msgid ""
"Qubes release is defined as specific versions of components, which are "
"developed more or less separately. Their versions are composed of major and "
"minor version of target Qubes OS release followed by third component which "
"is just incremented. There is no apparent indication that given version is "
"stable or not."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/releases/version-scheme.rst:92
#: 519856e0d50a4cce8ba06613961ad134
msgid ""
"There are some non-essential components like ``qubes-apps-*`` that are "
"shared between releases. Their versions indicate oldest qubes-release that "
"is supported. We try hard to support multiple releases by one branch to ease "
"code maintenance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/releases/version-scheme.rst:94
#: eb7f7fed44364a3197ce3109d4813887
msgid ""
"Different Qubes releases remixes may comprise of different components and "
"version are not guaranteed to be monotonic between releases. We may decide "
"that for newer release some component should be downgraded. There is no "
"guarantee that arbitrary combination of different versions of random "
"components will yield usable (or even install-able) compilation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/releases/version-scheme.rst:97
#: fb57313986224052bd54dda26bfde2cd
msgid "Git tags and branches"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/releases/version-scheme.rst:100
#: 0edd4ce6878e40a599fb603314d51501
msgid ""
"We mark each component version in the repository by tag containing "
"``v<version>``. Likewise, each Qubes OS release is marked by ``R<release>`` "
"tag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/releases/version-scheme.rst:102
#: b864117e23314431b314650cc71fee77
msgid ""
"At the release of some release we create branches named like ``release2``. "
"Only bug fixes and compatible improvements are backported to these branches. "
"These branches should compile. All new development is done in ``main`` "
"branch. This branch is totally unsupported and may not even compile "
"depending on maintainer of repository."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/releases/version-scheme.rst:104
#: a04dcd1558bc4277bc3539fd2e8b4cae
msgid ""
"All version and release tags should be made and signed by someone from ITL "
"staff. Public keys are included in ``qubes-builder`` and available at "
"https://keys.qubes-os.org/keys/."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/releases/version-scheme.rst:107
#: 3d3f2459950a43c5a2d6c2ddebabc865
msgid "Check installed version"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/releases/version-scheme.rst:110
#: 86ae62fef5bc4ec5972740e061aa2817
msgid ""
"If you want to know which version you are running, for example to report an "
"issue, you can either check in the Qubes Manager menu under ``About > Qubes "
"OS`` or in the file ``/etc/qubes-release`` in dom0. For the latter you can "
"use a command like ``cat /etc/qubes-release`` in a dom0 terminal."
msgstr ""
